  "prefLabel": "Env-A 3006.09 ERCs from Shutdowns",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-A 3006.09 ERCs from Shutdowns. ERCs which have been certified to, or emissions reductions which are eligible for certification to, a generator source which shuts down its production operations shall be public emissions credits and shall revert to the state for use consistent with this chapter, except where such ERCs are to be used at other stationary sources within the state by the person or persons who owned, operated and controlled the Generator source that was shutdown.\n\nSource. #6441, EXEMPT, eff 1-21-97",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-a3000.html"
}
